- DONE (2026-09-01) Structure ablation complete, job 3369038: 3 rungs x 169 = 507 runs, all exit 0.
  Full write-up in Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md 25. THE COMPOSITION PROGRAMME IS CLOSED.
  Two findings.
  (1) STRUCTURAL GUIDANCE THROUGH THE PROMPT DOES NOT WORK. Handing the model gold's tree moves
  shape adoption from 33% of cases to 30% (S1) and 27% (S2). Paired on the same 169 questions,
  133 are unchanged, 16 flip to correct and 20 flip to wrong -- churn, not effect. Mean predicted
  tree size 1.84 / 1.65 / 1.81 against gold's 2.51. Holds across two prompt formats: prose gave
  18% compliance (notes 24), a JSON scaffold in the dialect the model was fine-tuned to emit gives
  30% against an unhinted 33%. Not a formatting accident.
  Report the PER-CASE denominator. The report's first table divides by parsed predictions and
  reads 45% -> 36% -> 36%, which looks like a real decline; it is mostly an artefact of S1 parsing
  more queries (141 vs 121, schema-invalid 48 -> 28).
  (2) CORRECT STRUCTURE IS NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT. Conditioning on the model producing the
  right shape: F1 0.3855 (S0), 0.3614 (S1), 0.3353 (S2) -- roughly triple the 0.06-0.13 when the
  shape is wrong, so structure is a real lever, but ALL THREE sit below the 0.5148 trivial floor.
  With notes 23.7's observational 0.3770 at n=471 that is four independent estimates converging on
  ~0.35. A system that got the tree right every time would still score below a do-nothing query.
  Also worth keeping: the hint buys SYNTAX, not semantics. S1 raises execution 71.0% -> 81.1% and
  cuts schema-invalid 48 -> 28, while exact matches go 14 -> 13. That is the notes-21 syntax/
  semantics split reproduced inside one model under a controlled manipulation rather than inferred
  across arms -- the cleanest form of that claim the thesis has.
  NOT a finding: the unconditional F1 decline (0.1799 -> 0.1422 -> 0.1246). Paired on the 135
  discriminating questions the mean difference is -0.0377 (95% CI -0.0913..+0.0160) for S1 and
  -0.0553 (-0.1111..+0.0005) for S2. Both cross zero. Direction worth a sentence, effect not
  established -- reading the summary table alone would have produced an overclaim.

- CLOSED (2026-09-01) Everything bounded below the trivial floor, with the measurement that closed
  it. Do not reopen any of these without new evidence:
    * decoding-time selection (notes 22) -- oracle best-of-10 = 0.2464 < 0.5148
    * explicit schema linking (notes 23.3) -- already ~80% correct where it matters
    * constraint tuning / margin fixes (notes 23.2) -- errors are disjoint, not approximate
    * training rebalance toward compositional depth (notes 23.6, 25.5) -- bounded at ~0.35
    * decomposition, DIN-SQL / MAC-SQL style (notes 25.2, 25.5) -- the model does not take
      structural instruction, AND correct structure would not be enough if it did
  The one experiment that would make 25.5 causal rather than selected: force the structure
  programmatically -- build the tree from gold's skeleton in code and ask the model only for slot
  contents, so adoption is 100% by construction. Roughly half a day. Not built, because four
  agreeing estimates across two runs make it confirmatory; build it if a reviewer challenges the
  sufficiency claim.

- NEXT (2026-09-01, corrected 2026-09-02) GROUNDING is what is left. This entry originally said the
  model "never sees actual attribute VALUES"; that is wrong. `build_schema_block` at level `full`
  already emits attributes with bounded string-value enumerations and the E2O/O2O graphs with
  qualifiers. What it never emits is anything counted or instance-level: type counts, activity
  frequencies, relation cardinality, numeric ranges, the log timespan, or what its own query
  returns. Notes 23.3 shows it already knows WHICH types a question concerns; notes 25.5 shows
  that knowing the shape as well is still not enough. What is left is knowing what is in the log.
  See the AGENTIC WITH LOG-INSPECTION TOOLS entry parked above for the tool surface and the
  frontier-model caveat. It is also the only remaining direction that supplies the UPPER BOUND the
  paper still lacks -- right now there is a floor and no ceiling, which is precisely why the
  "cannot claim anything" critique lands.

- DONE (2026-09-02) RE-SCORING PASS: is part of the measured failure the instrument?
  ANSWER: partly, and it changes nothing. Full write-up in Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md
  26. Headline, fine-tuned arm, 135 discriminating entries, per-case means: strict 0.1825 ->
