  collapsed because of the resume bug fixed in notes 10, not because of the model).
  THE CENTRAL PROBLEM: data/finetune_ocpq.jsonl has JSON-ONLY targets (notes/TODO.md Q7). Fine-tuning
  a reasoning model on answer-only targets trains it to skip thinking, which yields a non-reasoning
  model on a different base. Three options, pick one and state it:
    E-a  fine-tune with thinking disabled, evaluate with thinking on    cheapest; train/test mismatch
    E-b  rejection-sampled self-traces: sample the base reasoning model on a 10-20k-row subset, keep
         traces whose final JSON equals the target, fine-tune on trace + JSON (STaR-style). The
         training data cannot be executed (not tied to logs), so the filter is exact JSON match.
         ~2-4 GPU-days of trace generation. Regenerating finetune_ocpq.jsonl needs instruction
         (CLAUDE.md 2.4) -- write traces to a NEW derived file instead.
    E-c  no fine-tuning: base reasoning model only                     answers "does reasoning help",
                                                                        not "does fine-tuning a reasoner"
  PIPELINE CHANGES, each behind a flag: strip <think> in parse_llm_json; generation_token_budget
  4000 -> 8-16k for this model; constrained decoding must leave the thinking span free and apply the
  grammar only after </think> (xgrammar structural tags, or two-phase generation); case_timeout_sec
  must rise -- CLAUDE.md 6 requires the cap on EVERY arm of a comparison, so run the reasoning model
  with its non-reasoning counterpart re-run at the same cap, or report it as its own table.
  temperature 0 is fixed by CLAUDE.md 2.1 but reasoning models are tuned for sampling and can loop
  under greedy -- keep greedy, measure and report the loop / budget-exhaustion rate; changing it
  needs explicit approval.
  TRAINING: traces push rows past max_seq_length 4096 -> 8192. Measured today at 4096: Llama 3.1 8B
  4.01 h, Ministral 3 14B 8.31 h (notes 04). At 8192 expect ~2x or more: 8B ~8-10 h (inside the 14 h
  wall), 14B ~17-20 h (needs checkpoint resume -- exactly where the notes-10 bug lived; re-test resume
  first).
  EVALUATION: reasoning generation is ~3-5x the tokens. The recommended scope is ONE model, base +
  fine-tuned, on the best cell (allowed-entities-only, schema on, constrained), 169 cases: ~2 x 169 x
  2-4 min ~= 11-23 GPU-h. The full per-model matrix equivalent would be ~30-125 GPU-h -- not in budget.
  TOTAL: ~3 weeks with E-b (1 week integration + tests, 2-4 days traces, 1-2 days training, 1 day eval,
  analysis). FEASIBILITY: MEDIUM for E-a/E-c, LOW-MEDIUM for E-b.
  WHAT THE EVIDENCE PREDICTS: the failure is semantic (notes 37.2) and arity choice is worse than a
  constant (notes 33.1), both decisions a reasoning step could plausibly improve. But prompted CoT on
  non-reasoning models did not help in matrix_full (chain-of-thought-plus below allowed-entities-only),
  so the prior is weak -- pre-register the effect needed (> ~0.03) before building.

- DECIDE (2026-09-14) TWO PROMPT GAPS, both of which move the pipeline fingerprint:
    * `throughputTime` is stored in SECONDS and rendered as `throughputTime (Float)` -- 3 of N2's 26
      link_mismatch cases write days (notes 36.3). A unit in the schema block is real missing information.
    * p2p attribute names carry SAP codes in parentheses, `_render_attribute` prints `name (Type)`, and
      the model strips the code (0 of 60,018 training examples show such a name) -- 2 gold cases, at
      most ~+0.006 F1 (notes 36.8). Quoting names would also diverge from the training format.

